90=424,430. Still not.\n\nAlternatively, if they did 978\u00d75=4,800 (instead of 4,890). Then total would be 391,200 +29,340=420,540 +4,800=425,340. Close but not.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they thought 978\u00d7400=391,200, but then 978\u00d735=34,230, but added 391,200 +34,230 as 425,430 but wrote 421,430 by mistake.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the user made a typo in their answer, but the correct answer is indeed 425,430.\n\nTherefore, the assistant should explain the correct calculation and point out the discrepancy.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>The product of 978 and 435 is **425,430**. Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n1. **Multiply 978 by 5 (units place):**  \n   \\[\n   978 \\times 5 = 4,\\!890\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 978 by 30 (tens place, shifted left by one digit):**  \n   \\[\n   978 \\times 3 = 2,\\!934 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2,\\!934 \\times 10 = 29,\\!340\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 978 by 400 (hundreds place, shifted left by two digits):**  \n   \\[\n   978 \\times 4 = 3,\\!912 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3,\\!912 \\times 100 = 391,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**  \n   \\[\n   4,\\!890 \\,+\\, 29,\\!340 \\,+\\, 391,\\!200 = 425,\\!430\n   \\]\n\n**Verification:**  \nUsing an alternative method:  \n\\[\n(1,\\!000 - 22) \\times 435 = 435,\\!000 - (22 \\times 435) = 435,\\!000 - 9,\\!570 = 425,\\!430\n\\]\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nThe correct answer is **425,430**, not 421,430. It appears there was an arithmetic error in the initial calculation.\n<\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 978 and 435 is **425,430**. Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n1. **Multiply 978 by 5 (units place):**  \n   \\[\n   978 \\times 5 = 4,\\!890\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 978 by 30 (tens place, shifted left by one digit):**  \n   \\[\n   978 \\times 3 = 2,\\!934 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2,\\!934 \\times 10 = 29,\\!340\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 978 by 400 (hundreds place, shifted left by two digits):**  \n   \\[\n   978 \\times 4 = 3,\\!912 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3,